# /etc/sudoers.d/pidvs-network
#
# Lets the box manage its OWN wireless connection: join a network the owner
# chose, forget one, and put up its own setup access point when it has none.
#
# This exists because the browser UI made WiFi load-bearing again. WiFi setup
# was deliberately removed on 2026-07-21, when BLE was the only control path
# and nothing a consumer did needed a network at all. That is no longer true:
# someone without the iOS app reaches the box over WiFi or not at all, and a
# box that cannot be put onto WiFi without a terminal is one they cannot use.
#
# Why sudo and not a polkit rule: NetworkManager refuses `wifi.share.open` and
# `wifi.share.protected` OUTRIGHT for a user with no local seat - "no", not
# "auth", so no password can satisfy it and a background service never will.
# The hotspot has to be created by root. Checked on the box, 2026-09-26.
#
# Scoped to ONE script with a fixed set of subcommands, not to `nmcli` with
# arbitrary arguments. Everything that could take the box off the air for good
# lives behind that script, which always leaves a way back - see its own
# header. A grant of `nmcli *` would not have that property.
#
# `__BOX_USER__` is a PLACEHOLDER for the box account, not a real user - provision.sh's substitute()
# rewrites it, and so does wifi-provision.js when it installs this on a box that provisioning can
# no longer reach. Same convention as every other file here; see provision.sh's own note.
#
# This lives under server/ rather than pi/ because a release tarball carries only server/, and the
# two boxes already in the field can be reached by nothing else.
#
# Install (provisioning does this for you):
#   sudo cp pidvs-network.sudoers /etc/sudoers.d/pidvs-network
#   sudo chmod 440 /etc/sudoers.d/pidvs-network
#   sudo visudo -c

__BOX_USER__ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/bin/pidvs-network status, /usr/local/bin/pidvs-network scan, /usr/local/bin/pidvs-network ap-up, /usr/local/bin/pidvs-network ap-down, /usr/local/bin/pidvs-network join *, /usr/local/bin/pidvs-network forget *
